# fixedbugs, defect 559, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's C0).
#
# `fill_int(@x: i64)` over `void fill_int(int *x)`, beside a module whose
# header defines `twice` of `long long` where this one's defines it of `int`.
# Each module's unit compiles its own header alone. Until 2026-10-10 the
# pointee check read every header of the program in one unit, which did not
# compile, and passed what it could not read: this built at exit 0 and C
# wrote four bytes into the eight, printing `11` where the binding is
# wrong. The same binding without the other module was refused. It is asked
# of this module's own header now, and refused the same either way.
use fixedbugs559/long_twice

extern "fixedbugs-559-int.h"
    function twice(x: i32) -> i32
    function fill_int(@x: i64)  #~ ffi_parameter_type

function main()
    y: i64 @= 0
    fill_int(@y)
    print(long_twice.doubled(x: 3) + y)
    print(twice(x: 4))
